Id: upd001w
Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: check_updates

Updates were installed that only take effect after a reboot: a new
kernel, or libraries that every running program already has loaded
(the C library, OpenSSL, systemd). Until the reboot the old versions,
with the holes the updates closed, keep running. The detail says how
it was found: /run/reboot-required (Debian and Ubuntu write it, with
the packages in /run/reboot-required.pkgs), the running kernel's
modules gone from /lib/modules (Arch, Alpine), or a newer kernel-core
installed than the one running (Fedora, RHEL).

To fix it, reboot at a convenient time. 'needs-restarting -r' (Fedora,
RHEL) and 'needrestart' (Debian, Ubuntu) also name the services that
can be restarted instead, for the updates that do not need a reboot.
